@flags
wrapper show_report version=1 id=b0000004-0004-0004-0004-000000000004

@prompt
Probes are for poking around. Drop them on different bindings to watch a program build up.

# Task
Set the new-moon bonus so the week totals **1800**, then explore.

**Explore**
- Probe `week` to see the subtotal (`1750`).
- You can also read a variable *without* probing it. Probe `watered`, then **right-click that sample** (a two-finger tap on a Mac trackpad, or Option-click) to open a dropdown of the values feeding it, including `week`.
- You never have to use the dropdown. Probing `week` directly works just as well. Two ways to see the same thing.

@hint
The new-moon bonus is 50.

@reference
### Probes
- **Add / remove a probe**: Cmd/Ctrl+E, or right-click then *Add probe*
- **See the variables**: right-click a sample (or Option-click) for the values feeding it

@hints
With the bonus set, the week totals 1800.

@code
let daily = 250 in
let week = daily * 7 in
let bonus = ¿ in
let watered = week + bonus in
watered

@test
test answer == 1800 end
